<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19314" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βάξις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>, ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βάζω</span>) poet. Noun,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>saying,</i> esp. <i>an
				oracular saying, inspired ulterance,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλύειν εὐηκέα β.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Emp.
					112.11
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐναργὴς β. ἦλθεν Ἰνάχῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					663
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεσφάτων β.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					87
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>report, rumour,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μιν . . β. ἔχει χαλεπή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Mimn.
					15
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">β. ἀργαλέη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					16
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεῶν ἐποπίζεο μῆνιν βάξιν τ᾽ ἀνθρώπων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thgn.
					1298
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">β. ἀλγεινήν, β. καλὴν λαβεῖν,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				494
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>El.</u>
				1006
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπείρειν ματαίαν β. ἐς πᾶσαν
				πόλιν</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				642
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				638
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διὰ δὲ πόλεας ἔρχεται β.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					224
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀξεῖα γάρ σου β. . . διῆλθ᾽
				Ἀχαιούς</span>
			<i>a report concerning</i> thee, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				998
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁλώσιμος β.</span>
			<i>tidings</i> of the capture, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				10
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θανόντος β. ἀνδρός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					351
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); so 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τήν τ᾽ ἀμφὶ Θησέως β.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					642
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>voice,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Epigr.Gr.
				989.2
			</span></i>.</div>
